quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  25,68,"And (they are) those who do not worship another god besides Allah, do not kill the soul that Allah has made inviolable, except in the lawful way, and do not commit adultery. And whoever does that shall face retribution."
  25,69,"The punishment shall be multiplied for him on the Day of Resurrection. And he shall abide in it with humiliation forever,"
  25,70,"except those who repent, believe and perform righteous deeds. For them, Allah will replace their evil deeds with good deeds. And Allah is Most Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  25,71,And whoever repents and acts righteously has truly turned to Allah with due penitence.
  25,72,"As for those who do not give false testimony, and when they come across some idle talk, they pass by (it) with dignity."
  25,73,"(They are) those who, when reminded of the signs of their Lord, do not turn a deaf ear and a blind eye to them,"
  25,74,"and those who say: ‘Our Lord! Grant us comfort in our spouses and our offspring, and make us a leading model for the God-conscious.’"
  25,75,"These (noble servants) shall be rewarded with elevated mansions (in Paradise) for their patience. And they shall be received there with greetings and (salutations of) peace,"
  25,76,abiding there forever. What an excellent place to settle and reside!
  25,77,"Say (to the disbelievers): ‘My Lord would not care for you even if your worship does not exist. But you have indeed rejected (the truth), so this (rejection) will (forever) continue as a permanent torment (for you).’"
